    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191192": {
      "title": "Student Lab Assistant - Dishwasher (Biochemistry)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03 Location: 2109 Adelbert Rd. Cleveland, OH 44106 Department of Biochemistry Lab Assistant- Student Worker List of Duties The Lab Assistant will support research laboratories in the Department of Biochemistry by: 1. Maintaining stocks ofclean laboratory glassware; this will include collecting glassware from individual laboratories, loading and unloading a Sterislaboratory glassware washer and sterilizer, and delivering clean glassware back to their home laboratories. 2. Sterilizing laboratory equipment, supplies, and materials, using Steris autoclaves. 3. Preparing media for cell culture; this includes preparing solutions and may involve autoclaving to sterilize the prepared media. 4. This position does require Lab Safety Training The student will be working around 10 -15 hours a week. Wage range for this position is: $13.44 - $13.92",
      "department": "School of Medicine (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173276": {
      "title": "Learning Support & Zoom Facilitation Assistant (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-11-07 Location: Peter B. Lewis  · Zoom Facilitation: o Set up and manage live Zoom sessions for classes, guest lectures, and workshops. o Monitor chat, breakout rooms, and recordings during sessions. o Provide real-time technical support to faculty and participants. o Take attendance for classes · Learning Material Accessibility: o Review and remediate course materials (PDFs, PowerPoints, Word documents, etc.) to ensure compliance with accessibility standards (WCAG 2.1, ADA). o Add alternative text (alt-text) to images, adjust document structure for screen readers, and verify caption accuracy on videos. o Collaborate with instructional designers or faculty to ensure updated materials meet accessibility best practices. · General Academic Support: o Maintain organized digital course archives and file structures. o Support faculty with minor updates to course content on Canvas or related platforms. o Provide feedback on usability and accessibility of online materials. Familiarity with Zoom video conferencing system, Adobe Acrobat, and Microsot Office Suite Please submit a current resume and cover letter. Your cover letter should highlight your experience as it relates to the duties of the position.",
      "department": "Weatherhead School of Management (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/166714": {
