    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185797": {
      "title": "One to One Fitness Office / Membership Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-16 Location: One to One Fitness Duties include, but are not limited to:  Process, update, and audit member and guest accounts  Process and audit point-of-sale transactions  Assist with payment requests, refunds, invoices, and auditing transactions  Assist with payment processing, deposits, payroll deduction payments  Create and manage electronic files  Data entry  Provide excellent and highly professional customer service in person, on the phone and via written and electronic communication  Assist and cover the front desk when needed  Other duties including copying, scanning, filing, organizing, running errands, etc. This pay rate begins at $15.75 an hour. Strong attention to detail a must  Strong aptitude in math and well developed reasoning skills  Excellent verbal, written, telephone, interpersonal and customer service skills  Strong organization skills with ability to multi-task, prioritize and give attention to detail in order to complete tasks and meet deadlines  Ability to follow protocols, manage time effectively and work on multiple projects simultaneously  Strong business ethics and standards  Strong proficiency with computers, spreadsheets, and word processing applications. Able to learn new software programs easily.  Demonstrated strong reliability.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185998": {
      "title": "Engagement Guide",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24 Location: Museum of Contemporary Art Cleveland (moCa Cleveland) GALLERY SECURITY & OPERATIONS: Learn, model, and apply museum philosophy, policies, and procedures with visitors and peer staff inside moCa’s galleries and other public spaces. Activate and deactivate exhibitions at the start and end of public hours. Monitor and maintain accessibility, appearance, and cleanliness of all galleries and public areas. Enforce security and safeguarding policies that ensure the safety of visitors, artworks, and spaces. Monitor for unintended changes in the condition of artwork on display. Monitor for environmental changes that may impact artwork conservation. Actively update and apply knowledge of moCa’s exhibitions, mission, events, facility, and emergency and incident procedures. VISITOR ENGAGEMENT: Initiate and lead interaction with diverse museum visitors using question-based, art object-focused methods about new, frequently changing material, ideas, and exhibitions. Participate in all learning workshops for exhibition content and engagement strategies. Cooperate with and model excellence in engagement strategies for peer Engagement Guides. Implement accessibility and equity policies, exhibit an openness to multiple forms of knowledge and experience, and regularly participate in a reflective professional practice. This position pays $14 hourly JOB SPECIFIC QUALIFICATIONS : Interest in education, museums, contemporary art, and/or culture Motivated, reliable, responsible, and professionally oriented Upholds obligations and follows established procedures Fluency in English with awareness and confidence in both verbal and non-verbal communication Computer competency and efficiency with Google Apps ESSENTIAL PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS : Communicate clearly with museum staff and visitors Able to work in a public-facing role Lift and move up to 15 lbs Positioned for extended periods of time on concrete floors Positioned for extended periods of time at a counter-height desk Operate a computer for extended periods of time Move quickly between various facility areas Apply through Interfolio.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186935": {
      "title": "Student Admin Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-03 Location: Thwing Center 153 $14.50 per hour (work-study) We are seeking a professional, energetic, and creative individual to join our office. This role involves collaborating with staff on various projects and contributing actively to the department's success. Key Responsibilities Coordinate projects and multitask effectively under varying demands. Perform general clerical duties, answering phones, checking voicemail,  including typing, data entry, printing, copying, preparing name badges, and monitoring inventory. Register and manage information within the D1 registration system. Exhibit initiative, strong problem-solving skills, and a highly collaborative approach. Software Experience Proficiency in Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and Adobe software. $14.50 per our (work-study) Some customer care experience is encouraged",
