    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188228": {
      "title": "OnBase Document Processing Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-27 Deadline: 2026-09-12 Location: Dental Research Building We are seeking a Graduate student to join out team for a part-time position of 20 hours per week. The hourly rate of pay is $13.50 per hours. The OnBse Document Processing Assistant supports SEO operations through the indexing, classification and form prepping and quality review of our digital hire forms. This positon helps ensure records are accurately captured, categorized and available for authorized business process. The student employee will work under the guidance of Student Employment staff and follow established procedures for ducment handling, indexing, quality assurance and records management. Th Essential Functions Review electronic documents and accurately identify the appropriate document classification. Enter and validate indexing information in accordance with established standards and procedures. Verify document quality, completeness, and legibility. Perform quality assurance reviews to ensure indexing accuracy. Prepare hiring forms in accordance with university policies and procedures to ensure students meet the eligibility requirements outlined in the job description. Maintain the confidentiality, security, and integrity of university records and sensitive information. Current enrollment at CWRU Strong attention to detail and accuracy Ability to follow documented procedures consistently Ability to maintain confidentiality when handling sensitive information Basic computer proficiency Strong organizational and time management skills Ability to work independently after training Reliable attendance and punctuality Please submit resume.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188827": {
      "title": "CWRU Community Pantry and Dean of Students Office - Student Employee",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05 Location: Dean of Students Office The CWRU Community Pantry Shift Supervisor is a student leadership position within the Dean of Students Office. This role supports the daily operations of the CWRU Community Pantry by overseeing pantry operations during assigned shifts, providing leadership to student employees, ensuring a welcoming environment for all visitors, and helping maintain an organized, safe, and efficient pantry. The Shift Supervisor serves as a role model for student employees and helps ensure exceptional customer service while maintaining the pantry's standards for organization, food safety, and professionalism. The CWRU Community Pantry provides free food, hygiene products, and household essentials to all students, faculty, staff, and community members. As part of the Dean of Students Office, the pantry contributes to a campus-wide community of care by reducing barriers to student success and promoting basic needs support. Responsibilities Direct and assist during stocking of shelves Lead sorting donations Unload boxes after a pick-up or delivery and guide organization Help with food pick-ups when needed Provide positive customer service to everyone who visits Assist with social media development Promote awareness of food insecurity on campus Participate in and contribute to team meetings Lead student workers in keeping the pantry clean and organized Supervise PantryTrak check-ins and maintain the pantry’s line Table at events to advertise the CWRU Community Pantry and the Dean of Students Office Complete temperature logs each shift Inspect food for quality assurance Complete inventory sheet and check for expiration dates Maintain privacy of all who use the pantry Check that after shift logs are completed by all student workers Oversee campus plate use for inventory tracking Supervise and recruit vo,unteers Hours Day and evening shifts available Shifts are 6 hours per week Expectations Attend all assigned tabling/marketing events Come to work with a positive attitude Notify the supervisor when a scheduled shift cannot be covered Complete all tasks assigned in a timely manner Arrive on time for scheduled shifts Treat everyone with respect and be polite to all Discrimination will not be tolerated Compensation $15.40hr (Federal Work-Study Students only) Minimum Skills Minimum commitment for 1 year Federal work-study student Working knowledge of Google Sheets Working knowledge of social media and platforms to create flyers and other media Creative and independent thinking Organizational capabilities Reliable and dependable Team player and leadership ability Ability to work with diverse populations with kindness and empathy Strong written and oral communication High level of customer service Ability to lift 20 pounds or more A passion for combating food insecurity Must be enrolled as a student at least half-time",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188836": {
      "title": "Student Customer Service Associate - Veale and Wyant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13 Location: Veale Center The Customer Service Associate (CSA) plays an essential role in creating a welcoming, safe, and efficient environment for all patrons using the recreation and athletic facilities. As the first point of contact, CSAs are responsible for delivering exceptional customer service while supporting the daily operations of both Veale Recreation and Athletic Center and the Wyant Athletic and Wellness Center. Key responsibilities include greeting patrons with a friendly and professional attitude, answering questions in person and over the phone, and providing facility tours and orientations to new visitors. CSAs assist patrons by issuing and collecting recreational equipment, conducting patron counts to monitor facility usage, and ensuring equipment is properly returned and organized. In addition to customer service duties, CSAs support facility operations by performing basic housekeeping tasks, such as folding towels, wiping down weight stations and benches, helping maintain clean and organized work areas, and assisting with various facility set-up and tear-down projects for programs and events, and building walkthroughs. CSAs are also expected to help maintain a safe environment by reporting hazards, following facility policies and procedures, and ensuring recreation spaces remain clean, organized, and ready for use. This includes returning equipment back to where it belongs in an orderly manner so that it is not a tripping hazard or in a way of another patrong using the facilty. Customer Service Associates are stationed at multiple locations throughout the recreation facilities, including the front control desk and issue desk in the Veale Recreation and Athletic Center, as well as the front control desk and basement weight room in the Wyant Athletic and Wellness Center. The position requires dependability, strong communication skills, attention to detail, and a commitment to providing outstanding service to all facility users. Applicants should communicate availability to supervisors on a regualr basis. The Customer Service Associate position is compensated at an hourly rate of $13.44 per hour . Please incluse resume in your application with a demonstrated interest in atheltics, health and fitness, sports, or hospitality. Please fill out if you are interested in working at both Veale and Wyant Athletic Centers. We cannot gaurantee hiring at one specific building. Please be patient with us as we review applicants for this role. Federal Work Study students prefered. Go Spartans!",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188879": {
      "title": "CWRU Community Pantry and Dean of Students Office - Student Employee",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05 Location: Dean of Students Office The CWRU Community Pantry and Dean of Students Office Student Employee will support the mission and foster the development and growth of the CWRU Community Pantry. The CWRU Community Pantry offers free resources such as perishable and shelf stable food items, hygiene products, and cleaning products. The CWRU Community Pantry is open to all students, faculty, staff, and community members. The Dean of Students Office oversees the CWRU Community Pantry and serves in an advocacy role for all CWRU students. Responsibilities Stock shelves Sort donations Unload boxes after a pick-up or delivery Help with food pick-ups when needed Provide positive customer service to everyone who visits Assist with social media development Promote awareness of food insecurity on campus Participate in team meetings Keep the pantry clean and organized Assist with PantryTrak check-ins and maintaining the pantry’s line Table at events to advertise the CWRU Community Pantry and the Dean of Students Office Assist with temperature logs when needed Inspect food for quality assurance Assist with inventory sheet and check for expiration dates Maintain privacy of all who use the pantry Other duties as assigned Hours Day and evening shifts available Shifts are 4-5 hours per week Expectations Attend all assigned tabling/marketing events Come to work with a positive attitude Notify the supervisor when a scheduled shift cannot be covered Complete all tasks assigned in a timely manner Arrive on time for scheduled shifts Treat everyone with respect and be polite to all Discrimination will not be tolerated Compensation $13.44hr (Federal Work-Study Students only) Minimum Skills Minimum commitment for 1 year Federal work-study student Working knowledge of Google Sheets Working knowledge of social media and platforms to create flyers and other media Creative and independent thinking Organizational capabilities Reliable and dependable Team player and leadership ability Ability to work with diverse populations with kindness and empathy Strong written and oral communication High level of customer service Ability to lift 20 pounds or more A passion for combating food insecurity Must be enrolled as a student at least half-time",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189074": {
      "title": "Information Systems Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-17 Deadline: 2026-09-21 Location: University Technology, UGEN Support  The Information Systems Assistant position provides an educational environment for a motivated student to develop and utilize relevant skills in computing to support the information system goals of staff and programs within University General (UGEN). The exact duties will be determined on an ongoing basis by the IT Engineer. Staff needs, current projects, and priorities will be considered when determining ongoing assignments. Assistants are expected to develop new skills during employment. Required Skills: Superiror communication skills (Verbal, In Person, Phone, and Written) Familiarity with the internal hardware of a computer Experience working with and solving problems with Windows/MacOS Prior knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite and Google Products (Chrome, Gmail, Drive, etc.) Experience with setting up and working with printers Daily Duties May Include: Clerical tasks in support of ongoing projects Telephone support/inquires for users in the supported areas Electronic mail support/inquires for users in the supported areas PC compatible hardware support Configuration of computing equipment in a networked environment Movement and installtion of computing equipment (lifting of up to 50 lbs. required) Working with hardware vendors to troubleshoot and repair hardware problems Providing software support for Microsoft Office Suite, Windows 11, Apple Operating Systems, Adobe Acrobat, or other software programs utilized by the staff Software installation following established guidelines for security and licensing Working with software vendors to troubleshoot and repair software problems Small project development and maintenance using appropriate software Create documentation and training materials for new and existing projects Additional responsibilites as assigned by appropriate staff Additional Oppurtunities: (Projects based on experience, knowledge, and time) Development of automated processes through Group Policy and/or scripting Development of new and existing software projects in C# or other appropriate languages Reporting Responsibilties: The information systems assistant reports directly to the IT Engineer. Additonal supervision will be provided by full-time staff in the UGEN & EXEC IT Support. Training: Assistants must complete training for the operation of the university vehicle. The UGEN & EXEC IT Support staff will provide appropriate technical training for new projects and responsibilities on a regular basis. Qualifications: Must hold a valid driver's license. Must have experience diagnosing and repairing computer-related hardware (CPUs, printers, monitors). Prior knowledge of Microsoft Windows and Office required. Compensation: $13.50/hour, up to 20 hours per week during Fall and Spring semesters. All Applicants MUST be Federal Work Study eligible. Please attach all resume materials below.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189179": {
      "title": "STUDENT POSITION-SIEGAL LIFELONG LEARNING BEACHWOOD OFFICE",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21 Location: Siegal Lifelong Learning-Beachwood The Siegal Lifelong Learning Program is seeking a reliable, organized, and enthusiastic Student Assistant to support the day-to-day operations of our educational programs and provide excellent service to our learners, instructors, and guest speakers. This position offers an opportunity to gain hands-on experience in program administration, event support, customer service, and educational day/evening programming in a welcoming and intellectually engaging environment. Key Responsibilities Assist with course and program registration , including helping students register and addressing registration questions. Answer and respond to phone calls and general inquiries from students and community members. Provide friendly, professional student support before and during courses and programs. Welcome students and direct them to classrooms and program locations . Assist with in-person program logistics , including preparing classrooms and making copies and other materials. Provide technical support for speakers and instructors , including setting up Zoom, presentations, microphones, and other audiovisual equipment. Assist with recording lectures and programs and distributing recordings and related materials to registered students. Help prepare and organize course materials, handouts, and other program resources . Assist with check-in and attendance at classes, lectures, and special events. Support the Lifelong Learning team with special projects and other program-related tasks as needed. This position provides an opportunity to work closely with an education-based program serving a diverse community of lifelong learners. The Student Assistant will gain experience in education, program coordination, event management, technology, and community engagement while contributing to the success of meaningful learning experiences. SALARY: Depending on experience and classification, starting at $13.44 to $15.00 Strong organizational and communication skills. Friendly, professional, and comfortable interacting with the older community; service-oriented for both instructors and community members. Reliable and able to work independently as well as part of a team. Comfortable learning and using basic technology, including Zoom and audiovisual equipment. Attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple tasks. Previous customer service, administrative, or event experience is helpful but not required. WORK STUDY PREFERRED MUST BE ABLE TO ATTEND OUR BEACHWOOD OFFICE -POSITION IS LOCATED IN BEACHWOOD Please include CV and relevant experience.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189679": {
      "title": "Sports Information Student Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13 Location: Various Athletic Facilities on Campus Student assistants in the sports information department support the efforts of the Associate Athletic Director for Communications and Media Relations as well as the Sports Information Director in publicizing the achievements of CWRU student-athletes and coaches. Student assistants are expected to serve in various event coverage roles. Typical tasks include but are not limited to: clerical work, sports writing, statistics, athletic photography, athletic video, and maintenance of athletics.case.edu. No formal training is required, but interest and/or knowledge in sports is preferred. Additional consideration will be given to students with specific skills in photo/video editing, Adobe Photoshop, Adobe InDesign, and usage of various popular social media platforms. Sports Information staff is stationed in the Veale Recreation and Athletic Center, along with various home competition venues around campus (depending on sport). Hourly wage is $13.44.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189749": {
      "title": "Departmental Assistant - UTech",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24 Location: PBL21 Under general supervision, this position is responsible for general office and basic technology support including proficiency in office productivity software (Google and Microsoft Office) to UTech North Campus  (Colleges of Law, Weatherhead School of Managment and MSASS). Duties include troubleshooting basic WEPA and other IT maintenance needs during standard business hours (M-F, 8:00am - 5:00 pm). $12.50 per hour 15-20 hours per week. Customer service, communication and organizational skills, Basic computer skills including working with documents and spreadsheets.   Must have consistent attendance. Software and hardware support experience preferred. Please provide a resume and schedule of availability for Fall 2026.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190011": {
      "title": "BRB Location: Food Service Worker/Utility (Student)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24 Location: BRB Cafe (Biomedical Research Building) Presents and serves food as needed. Maintains kitchen work areas and keeps equipment and utensils clean and orderly. Help with set up and clean up of work areas, including dishes, food service equipment and utensils. Replenishes condiments, beverages, and general supplies while maintaining service areas cleanliness. Carries pans, kettles and trays of food to and from workstations, stoves and refrigerators in accordance with safety standards. Utilizes approved food recipes and production standards to ensure proper quality, serving temperatures and standard portion control. Sweeps and mops floors to comply with safety and sanitation standards. Removes trash and places it into designated containers. Maintains kitchen work areas, equipment, worktables & other food prep surfaces; wash dishes, pans, utensils by hand and/or dish machine. Serves students and customers in a friendly, efficient manner following outlined steps of service. Relays relevant information to supervisor. Ensures compliance with company service standards and with all sanitation and safety standards. Performs other duties as assigned. Starting Hourly Rate: $15.00 Qualified candidates must be able to perform the essential functions of this position satisfactorily with or without a reasonable accommodation. This job post is not necessarily an exhaustive list off all essential responsibilities, skills, tasks or requirements associated with this position. While this is intended to be an accurate reflection of the position posted, Bon Appetit reserves the right to modify or change the essential functions of the job based on business necessity. Previous food service experience preferred. Please include a cover letter listing your past food service experience.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
