    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190015": {
      "title": "Cashier / Barista",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24 Location: Spartie Mart, Starbucks, Dunkin Performs cashier duties if needed, using the Point-of-Sale system, according to established procedures as well as maintaining cash accuracy with receipts. Prepares espresso orders for customers using standard measures and recipes. Enters orders accurately into POS device; accepts cash and charge payments. Replenishes condiments, beverages and general supplies while maintaining cleanliness of service area. Ensures proper presentation, portion control and maintenance of proper serving temperatures; follows HACCP standards. Maintains sanitation and orderliness of all equipment, supplies and utensils. Greets customers courteously and interacts in a manner to ensure customer satisfaction. Relays relevant concerns from customers to supervisors. Serves customers quickly and efficiently, and prevents delays in serving lines. Maintains professional appearance at all times, clean and well groomed in accordance with company standards. Starting Hourly Rate: $15.00 Must be able to preform the essential functions with or without any reasonable accommodation. This is not necessarily an exhaustive list of all essential responsibilities, skills or tasks. The Company reserves the right to modify or change the essential functions of the job as needed.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190075": {
      "title": "Box Office Student Staff",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21 Location: Maltz Performing Arts Center The Box Office Assistant serves as a welcoming, knowledgeable, and professional point of contact for guests attending events at the Maltz Performing Arts Center (MPAC). As one of the first people guests encounter, this position plays an important role in creating a positive experience from the moment patrons arrive through the end of the event. Box Office Assistants support event operations by preparing the box office and lobby, assisting guests with ticketing and general questions, addressing concerns, and providing excellent customer service. Events take place on weekdays, weeknights, and weekends, and this position requires flexibility to work a variety of event schedules. Starting salary: $13.50/hour with yearly raises Federal Work Study Not Required Hours: Flexible, Nights, Weekends In-Person, on-site What Success Looks Like A successful Box Office Assistant helps every guest feel welcomed, informed, and taken care of. They are attentive to what is happening around them, communicate clearly, respond to problems quickly and professionally, and understand that they are an important part of the guest experience at the Maltz Performing Arts Center. Excellent customer service and interpersonal skills. Friendly, welcoming, and professional demeanor. Strong verbal communication and active listening skills. Ability to remain calm, patient, and professional when handling difficult or unexpected situations. Ability to exercise good judgment and know when to resolve an issue independently and when to escalate it. Strong attention to detail and accuracy when handling ticketing and financial transactions. Ability to learn and follow Maltz Performing Arts Center and Case Western Reserve University policies and procedures. Ability to learn ticketing systems, event procedures, and venue operations. Ability to work independently while also functioning effectively as part of a team. Ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities in a busy event environment. Flexibility and willingness to assist with a variety of event-related duties. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and varying event schedules. Ability to stand and remain active for extended periods during events. Previous customer service, box office, theater, performing arts, hospitality, or event experience is helpful but not required.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190165": {
      "title": "Box Office Student Employee Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21 Location: Maltz Performing Arts Center The Student Employee Coordinator (the “Coordinator) reports to the Assistant Director of Box Office & Venue Marketing (“Supervisor”) and is responsible for regular communications with the rest of the Student Box Office Assistants (the “Team”). The Coordinator will work and meet with the Supervisor to allocate work slots for the Team for upcoming weeks. They will provide summaries of the available slots to the Team on a weekly basis. They may also be tasked with helping the Maltz Performing Arts Center (MPAC) staff find solutions to various problems. The Coordinator will also help maintain the student roster by gathering information from the Team members on a semesterly basis. They should be familiar with student life on campus and be able to help guide the Supervisor around the nuances of the CWRU academic calendar. They will also assist in other administrative roles and continue Box Office responsibilities as deemed necessary. Serving as key setup and teardown staff for the Box Office, this role is charged with operating the ticketing system before and during events at the Maltz Performing Arts Center. Operations include printing and handing out will call, selling tickets, and finding patron orders in the ticketing system. The role is also a part of  the safe and proper delivery of an exceptional customer experience that lives up to and exceeds front-facing customer expectations. This role requires night and weekend availability based on event schedules with work hours ranging from 8-16 hours per week. Starting salary: $14.00/hour with yearly raises Federal Work Study, Not Required Hours: Flexible, Nights, Weekends In-Person, on-site Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: ● Selling, processing, and organizing ticket sales before and during each event; ● Printing, organizing and handing out will call tickets prior to the show; ● Helping patrons with any ticket/ticket system questions; ● Receiving complaints and addressing/escalating as appropriate from guests; ● Processing ticketing/transaction processing; ● Collecting and verifying patron and client contact information, and ensuring that information is up to date in all ticketing systems, email service providers, and customer databases; ● Other responsibilities as requested and expanded for this role. Ability to work nights and weekends as needed A thorough understanding of campus and center policy and procedure; Effective and engaging communication skills and ability to speak and listen to high-caliber guests and clients; Friendly and out-going personality; A sense of urgency in resolving issues, problems and errors in the delivery of an exceptional experience to our guests and clients; Ability to work autonomously and manage multiple tasks simultaneously; Ability to analyze situations and develop solutions;",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190202": {
      "title": "Digital Humanities Research Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20 Location: Baker-Nord Institute for the Humanities and Kelvin Smith Library The Baker Nord Institute for the Humanities, Dr. Ben Vinson III (historian), and Mr. David Beales from the Freedman Digital Scholarship Center are hiring students with strong techn ology skills to develop and deploy a transformer-based OCR and text analysis pipeline, called BEN4. The SOMOS project applies open source AI tools to make specific repositories within the Mexican National Archives machine readable. The project then analyzes the machine readable text with cutting-edge, best practices in text analysis. Students will be hired as Class III student employees. Starting pay will be $14.52-$15.40/hr The goal is to create a unique, adaptable, and highly effective digital/AI tool that can be used by humanists for any collection of interest.  Accordingly, the project uses a modular design that allows different small models with context relevant training to be plugged into the pipeline as needs change. The SOMOS project will offer opportunities to collaborate with partners in other institutions as we test models and work towards deploying the SOMOS-BEN4 pipeline in support of other collections. We are looking for members to constitute the SOMOS team who have interest or expertise in some or all of the following areas: Deploying open source AI/ML models using Ollama and Python Optimizing systems for local hardware and cloud deployments Evaluation and fine-tuning of LLMs Computer vision, TrOCR, HTR and Image Preparation GraphRAG, Topic Modelling, Named Entity Recognition and other text analysis methods Web stack and UX/UI Given the wide variety of experimental technological resources used in this project, an exceptional capacity for self-directed learning with technology is paramount. Additionally, given that the historical collections we are working with are in Spanish, we are also looking for students who have intermediate to advanced reading knowledge of Spanish and demonstrate a willingness to learn colonial Spanish.  It is not necessary, however, for students to have both the technological expertise and Spanish language skills. Please sumbit a resume and short cover letter describing your interest in the position using the tools in interfolio. If you ahve any questions about the position that you would like answered before applying, please contact Digital Scholarship Librarian David Beales roger.beales@case.edu or Dr. Ben Vinson ben.vinson@case.edu .",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190209": {
      "title": "Marketing/Communications and Web Content Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21 Location: Adelbert Hall The Marketing/Communications and Web Content Assistant will support marketing and communications directors across Case Western Reserve University in making important website updates, creating new web pages, text editing, image placement, and creation of web analytics reports. This individual also may support the directors in a range of other marketing and communications projects, including analytics and reporting. Must have strong interpersonal skills, work well with others, and communicate professionally with colleagues and the university community. Pay rate: $14/hour QUALIFICATIONS Pursuing a degree in Marketing, English, Computer Science or a related field. Competent proofreading and editing skills. Excellent time management, customer service, organizational, and communication skills. Capacity to handle multiple responsibilities and prioritize projects to stay on top of workflow and strict deadlines. Proficiency with Google Suite. Experience with content management systems is preferred but not required. HTML experience is preferred but not required. Please submit your resume (required) and, if available, any examples of web or marketing/communications projects (including writing/editing) you have done (not required).",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190234": {
      "title": "Student Web Content and Graduate Enrollment Marketing Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24 Location: University Marketing and Communications The Web Content and Graduate Enrollment Marketing Assistant will work with the University Marketing and Communications web team and graduate and professional enrollment marketing team to gain hands-on experience supporting the university's websites and enrollment marketing campaigns. Responsibilities include updating website content, creating and formatting web pages, editing text, and selecting and placing images, as well as supporting digital campaign work such as presentation creation and organizing photo/video assets. The ideal candidate is curious, detail-oriented, and eager to learn, with strong interpersonal and communication skills and is comfortable moving between web production tasks and enrollment marketing support. Hourly rate: $14 and Class III Ability to work independently Strong attention to detail Strong communications (written and verbal) skills Ability to meet deadlines Desire to learn new skills Proficiency with Google Suite Experience with content management systems is preferred but not required HTML experience is preferred but not required Applicants must submit a resume and cover letter.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190394": {
      "title": "Alumni/development content assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24 Location: University Marketing & Communications This individual will help execute a variety of content-related tasks, including technical and routine functions as well as creative and communication-based projects. The individual will work closely with the development and alumni communications team on ensuring storytelling is reaching our audience on a variety of platforms. Day-to-day responsibilities will vary, but can include building web stories, scheduling and creating posts for the Alumni Association channels, creating templated copy for emails or event registrations and updating content calendars. The student employee can expect to gain experience working on development and alumni marketing and communications pieces, focusing on digital engagement and marketing. The salary for this position is $14 per hour. Required skills: Ability to work independently Strong attention to detail Strong communication skills (written and verbal) Familiarity with primary social media platforms Preferred skills: HTML experience WYSIWYG interface experience Photography and/or videography skills Applicants must submit a resume and cover letter.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190442": {
      "title": "Social Media Office Assistant – UMC",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24 Location: University Marketing and Communications This individual will help execute a variety of social media-related tasks, including technical and routine functions as well as creative and communication-based projects. The individual will work closely with the social media team in office to collaborate on compiling and drafting posts across the university’s social media pages, trend research, community engagement, social listening, engagement with social media ambassadors and the like. Day-to-day responsibilities will vary. Occasional evening and weekend hours may be required for event coverage and general campus photography. The student employee can expect to gain experience working on marketing and communications pieces, including social media copy, photography and videography, audience engagement and brand health assessments. The wage for this position is $14/hour. Required skills: Photography and videography skills Ability to work independently Strong attention to detail Strong communication skills (written and verbal) Familiarity with primary social media platforms Applicants must submit a resume and a document with 2-3 creative samples (photo/video content, captions, etc.). If you have any issues with uploading photo and video samples, you may submit them to socialmedia@case.edu . Be sure to include your full name and the position for which you are applying.",
      "department": "UGEN (STUDENT)"
    },
